body:
`hideColumn` removes the column from state but doesn’t clear `sortColumn`/`sortDirection` when the hidden column is currently sorted. This can leave the table sorted by an invisible column. Consider resetting sort state when hiding the active sort column.
```suggestion
    setColumns(prev => prev.filter(c => c.accessorKey !== columnKey));

    // If we are hiding the currently sorted column, reset sort state
    if (sortColumn === columnKey) {
      setSortColumn(null);
      setSortDirection(null);
    }
```
